A||||5||ToddAsh||Rear strut /spring noise||||1||
Z||000000||ToddAsh||04-18-2001||07:17 PM|||| I'm hearing a clip-clop kind of noise when I go over bumps mostly in the left rear.The struts are new and the car only has 16,000 miles on it.The strut pad(or whatever the thing is at the top of the strut looked good but maybe I missed something.Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated.I'm gonna jack it up and look at it tomorrow night. Todd ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-18-2001||07:24 PM||||hard to say..... a likely culprit is the brake pad clip for the inboard pad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||04-18-2001||08:52 PM||||Todd, I second what ogre said. Have you done rear brake work recently? The inner brake pads on the rear of my '87 6000 STE (similar to Fieros) rattled when driving over small bumps.  I just could not believe what a racket the pads made, especially with the sunroof open.  The fix was simple. Just bend the four little fingers slightly on that stainless steel ring that hold the inner pad to the piston. They should be snug on the inner pad backing plate. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||04-19-2001||12:50 AM||||Might be the spring clunking too. In 85, they had to add a rubber tube over the top of the spring to fill the gap on some cars. <P>Clunk-Clunk fix.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ToddAsh||04-19-2001||09:49 PM|||| Yep it's definitly in the spring not the brakes.Is there a way to fix this without taking off the struts? Just got it aligned and the highway handling is really great.Thanks, Todd||||reg||1
Z||000005||ToddAsh||04-19-2001||09:51 PM|||| But maybe it is the brakes.I'll make sure tomorrow night. Thanks for all the help. Todd Ash||||reg||1
